# Line endings are frozen as committed, deliberately.
#
# This tree is mixed: modules/nameplates.lua is stored CRLF, CHANGES-octo.md is
# stored LF, and that is inherited from upstream rather than chosen. Without this
# file git converts on checkout, so the working copy stops matching the blob and
# an ordinary edit can come back as a whole-file diff instead of the three lines
# you changed -- which is exactly what happened while editing CHANGES-octo.md.
#
# "-text" disables end-of-line conversion entirely: checkout gives back the bytes
# that were committed, and commits store the bytes on disk. Nothing renormalises.
#
# The alternative, "* text=auto eol=lf", is tidier in the abstract but would
# rewrite every file in one commit. This fork merges from brues-code/pfUI
# regularly, and a mass renormalisation would collide with every future sync.
* -text
